    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling performance today, spearheaded by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our top daily efficiency score of 83.29. **Henderson** draws a favorable matchup against Lugo with significant park factors (+16%) and a strong platoon advantage boosting his output. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (75.20) and **Jacob Wilson** (74.08) are elite starts, with **Wilson** specifically benefiting from a high-target matchup against Schultz (5.23 xERA) and the efficiency gains of hitting out of the lead-off spot. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Andy Pages** also project as core contributors, both eclipsing the 70-point threshold by leveraging strong SP-skill advantages against M\u00e1rquez and Bratt, respectively.\n\nWhile the primary lineup is optimized for maximum run production, the decision to bench **Brayan Rocchio** was our tightest call of the day. Despite a solid 59.25 score\u2014bolstered by a favorable SP skill rating\u2014**Rocchio** ultimately fell short of the threshold required to displace the high-ceiling versatility of **Jackson Merrill** or the platoon-heavy upside of **Josh Lowe**. **Lowe** remains a priority start despite hitting lower in the order, as his favorable matchup against Bradley and the situational boost provided by a \"slow delivery\" opposing pitcher significantly improve his stolen base probability, a critical metric for our scarcity-weighted strategy.\n\nManagers should monitor the wind in the **Drake Baldwin** start; while his score of 51.25 keeps him in the lineup, the \"Wind In\" advisory (-5%) effectively caps his power upside today. We are also keeping a close eye on **Josh Lowe** and **Jackson Merrill**, both of whom are projected to benefit from their respective opponents' slower delivery times to the plate, potentially unlocking the stolen base production we prioritize. Despite the risk inherent in facing elite arms, the depth of our bench\u2014featuring high-xwOBA options like **Miguel Vargas**\u2014ensures we have immediate pivots should any of the primary lineup slots fail to confirm their projected batting orders.",
